    "scope": "Frozen local Windows received-digest metadata query/receiver/client validation using actual owned TCP/TLS, SQLite and captured source; separate actual Windows OS-credential sender and full TLS receiver/client/remote-query CLI gates. No source verification or semantic reasoning is claimed. Configured public deployment, automatic historical acquisition, proprietary service equivalence and full platform/STATUS acceptance remain open."
  },
  "findings": [
    "Deterministic literal metadata queries process explicitly selected accepted packets on read. Both the receiver host and the current matching principal grant must independently allow query. Old grants default to false; intake/receipt behavior remains available without query permission. Local CLI uses an existing-only read-only Store; remote CLI reads only the service token and no sender Store or App signing key.",
    "All 1-32 selected proposal IDs are scoped before producing any page. Current endpoint, principal, App, sender workspace, installation and repository must match. Missing/foreign selection refuses atomically rather than returning a complete empty result. Authentication precedes body acquisition; revoked grants during upload refuse before query replay. Protocol bodies cannot widen host rights.",
    "Row identities bind immutable receipt, row family and original JSON pointer. Duplicate symbols, repeated parent edges and original observation ordinals remain distinct. Commit parents, source-association claims, replies and review membership retain directed typed relations. Presence lookup is explicitly limited to the original received digest or captured thread, never local Git/source truth.",
    "Results retain sender coverage/omissions and false source-authority/semantic-identity flags. Metadata byte/line positions remain sender claims; the receiver anchor is only the packet JSON pointer. Literal case-sensitive Unicode matching over canonical metadata/context, pagination/counts and independent work/search/output limits introduce no model calls, source capture/execution or derived record writes. Complete remains false.",
    "Native HTTP client validates closed protocol/request/scope/count/receipt-qualified row bindings, row-kind-specific pointers and false authority flags before publishing one response. Host-selected CA adds trust without disabling hostname validation; no retries, redirects, proxy fallback or production credentials over plaintext HTTP are added.",
    "Nine additional default actual-socket/SQLite/CLI cases and two protocol/request unit regressions cover Unicode pagination, duplicate/parallel directed evidence, all-or-nothing scope, default query denial, current revocation during partial body, exact work/search/output boundaries, caller transaction/SQL policy restoration, corrupted storage/expiry and unchanged logical records/source counts.",
    "The separate actual Windows OS credential/TLS gate now runs real receiver, approved sender recovery and remote query CLI processes over owned TLS. Three unique token/TLS/signing credentials are created and removed. One intake survives local sender acknowledgment failure, GET reconciles it and a third POST queries metadata from an empty cwd with a nonexistent App signing credential. No system roots, private key files, public deployment or real GitHub writes are involved.",
    "Original inventory identities, unreconciled rows, backend runtime unknowns and false full-contract certifications are retained. Configured public production, remote source verification, semantic reasoning, automatic historical acquisition, live App installation/deployment, whole-platform/STATUS acceptance and proprietary upstream equivalence remain open. Prior OS1314 fixture failures are not accepted by this scoped run."
  ],
  "developmentAttempts": {
    "r1": "20 default receiver/query cases passed, one actual OS-credential gate ignored by default. Follow-up added strict response pointer/envelope validation, typed relation-field refusal, HTTP packet reservation, local CLI/state checks and partial-body revocation/expiry/corruption regressions.",
    "r2": "See raw receipts/logs: library plus 23 default receiver/query cases, separate actual receiver/sender/recovery/query CLI TLS gate and all-target Clippy. These overlapping counts are not added to the final totals."
